%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Original Payment stays SUCCESS until REC-05 confirms actual refund. No automatic bank transfer is performed.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Member
    participant UI as CancelSubscription
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as subsController
    participant S as subscriptionsService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Confirm cancellation of own paid subscription
    UI->>API: PATCH /api/v1/subscriptions/:id/cancel
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorize(MEMBER), validate request
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: cancelSubscriptionBySelf(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: cancelSubscriptionBySelf(id, userId, reason)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Read subscription owner, original collected payment and current remaining days
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Require own cancellable paid subscription
        S->>S: SCHEDULED refund 100 percent, ACTIVE with ceil daysLeft above 15 requests 30 percent of original collected amount, otherwise zero
        alt missing, wrong owner, FREE or non-cancellable state
            S-->>C: 400 / 403 / 404 / 409
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Locked transaction CAS subscription CANCELLED, revoke source rights and record positive refund request
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S-->>C: Cancelled subscription and requested refund estimate
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error

